### 3.3.1 Phase 2D MVP HTTP surface (shipped)

Manifest-driven routes on `/wallet/*` (mirror `/finance/*` prefix convention). Registered only on `wallet-ws1` certification fixture; Denali and other production workspaces remain route-inaccessible (`WALLET_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED`).

| Method | Path                                          | Actor                          | Idempotency-Key |
| ------ | --------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------ | --------------- |
| `GET`  | `/wallet/me/balance`                          | member (session-derived scope) | —               |
| `GET`  | `/wallet/me/transactions`                     | member (session-derived scope) | —               |
| `GET`  | `/wallet/accounts/:accountId/balance`         | member (own account)           | —               |
| `GET`  | `/wallet/accounts/:accountId/transactions`    | member (own account)           | —               |
| `GET`  | `/wallet/accounts`                            | operator (`admin` \| `owner`)  | —               |
| `POST` | `/wallet/accounts/:accountId/credit`          | operator                       | required        |
| `POST` | `/wallet/accounts/:accountId/debit`           | operator                       | required        |
| `POST` | `/wallet/transactions/:transactionId/reverse` | operator                       | required        |

**Handler pipeline (strict order):**

1. Resolve tenant context (`TenantAuthContext` from JWT — never from body).
2. Resolve workspace context (`workspaceId` on member auth; operator tenant scope).
3. `WalletCapabilityPort.assertEnabled(tenantId)` — workspace support + module enablement.
4. Member entitlement (`member.module.wallet`) or operator role (`admin` \| `owner`, `ACTIVE`).
5. Validate request DTO (`wallet-http-contracts` Zod parsers).
6. Require `Idempotency-Key` header on mutations; hash body for HTTP idempotency relay.
7. Invoke `WalletService` → `wallet-core` application services via host repository.
8. Map stable domain errors (`WALLET_*`) — never Prisma/stack traces.
9. Return safe read models (derived balance, immutable transaction history).

**Idempotency:** HTTP `Idempotency-Key` + request hash → `creationIdempotencyKey` + `commandFingerprint` in `wallet_transactions`. Same key + same fingerprint replays; same key + different fingerprint → `WALLET_IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`.

**Response safety:** String minor-unit amounts only; no raw ledger-entry mutation endpoints; no synthetic finance booking wallet ids; no internal tenant-resolution fields in JSON.

