## 4. Authorization boundary (recommended)

Layered fail-closed model — same separation as finance:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A[HTTP / Portal request] --> B{Tenant resolved?}
  B -->|no| X401[401/403]
  B --> C{workspaceWallet supported + module enabled?}
  C -->|no| XW[WALLET_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED / FORBIDDEN_WALLET_MODULE_DISABLED]
  C --> D{Surface}
  D -->|member| E{member.module.wallet entitled?}
  E -->|no| XE[MemberModuleUnauthorized / 403]
  E --> F{Member workspaceId matches?}
  D -->|operator| G{admin or owner?}
  G -->|no| XO[FORBIDDEN_OPERATOR_FORBIDDEN]
  F --> H[WalletService + tenant RLS]
  G --> H
```

| Layer                        | Owner        | Mechanism                                                                                  |
| ---------------------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Module enablement**        | API host     | `WalletCapabilityPort.assertEnabled(tenantId)` — mirror `FinanceCapabilityPort`            |
| **Member entitlement**       | API + portal | `evaluateMemberPortalEntitlements` + `portalModuleGrants`; portal `isMemberModuleEntitled` |
| **Operator role**            | API host     | `assertWalletOperatorAccess` — `admin` \| `owner`, `ACTIVE`, tenant scope                  |
| **Tenant scope**             | All layers   | `tenantId` on auth context; `withTenantRls` / ALS alignment                                |
| **Workspace scope (member)** | Member APIs  | `workspaceId` required for `role === member` (`tenant-kernel.ts`)                          |
| **Direct URL / API**         | Fail closed  | Portal: unauthorized component; API: stable error codes before business logic              |

**Not in scope Phase 0:** CASL subjects for wallet (today CASL is Tour-only in `api-ability.ts`). Wallet should use dedicated `WalletAuthorizationPort`, not extend Tour CASL.

---

## 5. Database and RLS invariants (Phase 2C tables)

Shipped tables: `wallet_accounts`, `wallet_transactions`, `wallet_ledger_entries` (Prisma migration `20260902120000_wallet_member_accounts_rls`).

Mandatory for any Wallet schema PR:

| Invariant             | Requirement                                                                                                                                                           |
| --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **tenant_id**         | `UUID NOT NULL` on every wallet table; FK to `tenants`                                                                                                                |
| **Ownership**         | Member accounts: `tenant_id` + `user_id` + `workspace_id`; operator mutations record `actor_user_id`                                                                  |
| **RLS**               | `ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY` + `FORCE`; policy `tenant_id = current_setting('app.current_tenant_id', true)::uuid` (see `infra/sql/008_finance_payments_delta.sql`)     |
| **Immutable ledger**  | Append-only `wallet_ledger_entries` (or equivalent); no UPDATE/DELETE on posted entries; corrections via reversing entries                                            |
| **Balance authority** | Published balance is **derived** from the sum of posted entries per account; no authoritative mutable `balance` column (optional snapshots must reconcile to entries) |
| **Idempotency**       | `creation_idempotency_key` + `@@unique([tenantId, creationIdempotencyKey])` on mutating aggregates; HTTP `Idempotency-Key` hashing pattern from finance               |
| **Concurrency**       | Balance-affecting mutations run in `prisma.$transaction` + `withTenantRls`; serialize per account (e.g. advisory locks)                                               |
| **Audit**             | `audit_events` and/or wallet-specific audit append-only table for operator adjustments                                                                                |
| **Currency**          | `currency VARCHAR(8)` per account or entry; amounts as **string integer minor units** (finance convention)                                                            |
| **ALS alignment**     | All writes inside `runWithTenantContext` + `assertActiveTenantMatchesRlsTarget`                                                                                       |

**Out of scope for wallet tables:** Reusing `payments`, `finance_refunds`, or `outbox_events` as the member wallet ledger (integration only).

