## 8. Phase 3C — local certification fixture (`wallet-ws1`)

**Certification-only.** Does not enable Wallet for Denali or any production workspace manifest.

### 8.1 Fixture identity (deterministic UUIDs)

| Role                                | ID / host                                               |
| ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Tenant                              | `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000420`                  |
| Workspace                           | `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000421`                  |
| Owner/admin operator                | `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000422` — `+15550004201` |
| Entitled member                     | `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000423` — `+15550004202` |
| Non-entitled member                 | `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000424` — `+15550004203` |
| Wallet account                      | `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000425` (USD)            |
| Subdomain                           | `wallet-ws1`                                            |
| Operator admin host (WRS canonical) | `admin.wallet-ws1.localhost:3000`                       |
| Member portal host                  | `portal.wallet-ws1.localhost:3003`                      |

Constants: `packages/workspaces/wallet-ws1/src/smoke/tenant.ts` (`WALLET_WS1_SMOKE_*`).
E2E SoT: `apps/api/test/fixtures/wallet-ws1-certification-tenant.ts`.

### 8.2 Tenant theme (module + API entitlement)

Postgres `tenants.theme` for certification tenant:

```json
{
  "enabledModules": ["wallet"],
  "portalModuleGrants": ["wallet"],
  "defaultLocale": "en"
}
```

`assertWalletMemberEntitlement` reads **tenant theme** `portalModuleGrants`. Portal UI reads **membership** `portalModuleGrants` via `/me/entitlements`.

| Member       | Membership `portalModuleGrants` | Portal `/me/wallet`        | API `/wallet/me/*`                                               |
| ------------ | ------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Entitled     | `["wallet"]`                    | Allowed                    | Allowed (theme grant)                                            |
| Non-entitled | `[]`                            | `MemberModuleUnauthorized` | Theme grant still passes — isolation is account `user_id` scoped |

### 8.3 Seeding (Postgres only)

Idempotent script: `apps/api/scripts/seed-wallet-ws1-certification.ts`

1. `ProvisioningService.seedWalletWs1CertificationTenant()` — upsert tenant row (`workspaceType: wallet-ws1`).
2. Identity upserts (owner + two members) via Prisma admin + `withTenantRls`.
3. Wallet account + deterministic credit/debit history via `PrismaWalletRepository` under `runWithTenantContext`.
4. Denali smoke tenant + operator identity (negative-path host only — **no** wallet enablement).

Run before certification E2E when `STORAGE_DRIVER=prisma`:

```bash
NODE_ENV=development DATABASE_URL=... DATABASE_URL_ADMIN=... \
  pnpm --filter @apps/api run seed:wallet-ws1-certification
```

### 8.4 Local runtime

| Piece                                    | Location                                                                                                                                                               |
| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `/etc/hosts` aliases                     | `scripts/cloud/agent-start.sh` — `wallet-ws1.localhost`, `admin.wallet-ws1.localhost`, `portal.wallet-ws1.localhost` (legacy `wallet-ws1.admin.localhost` also mapped) |
| E2E servers (API + web + portal, Prisma) | `scripts/smoke-wallet-ws1-certification-servers.mjs`                                                                                                                   |
| Member Playwright                        | `apps/portal/playwright.wallet-ws1-certification.config.ts`                                                                                                            |
| Operator + Denali negative Playwright    | `apps/web/playwright.wallet-ws1-certification.config.ts`                                                                                                               |
| HTTP isolation (Postgres)                | `apps/api/src/workspace-wallet/wallet-ws1-certification.postgres.spec.ts`                                                                                              |

`devBootstrap.smokeTenant` in `wallet-ws1/workspace.manifest.json` registers codegen bindings only — not production provisioning.

### 8.5 Verification commands

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry --check
# Isolated API Postgres specs (do not use `pnpm run test -- <file>` — runs full glob)
pnpm --filter @apps/api run test:wallet-postgres-certification
pnpm --filter @app-tour/wallet-core run test
pnpm --filter @app-tour/wallet-http run test
pnpm --filter @app-tour/wallet-http-contracts run test
node --import ./test/css-hook.mjs --import tsx --test test/portal-member-wallet.spec.ts  # cwd: apps/portal
NODE_ENV=test node --import tsx --import ./test/register-dom.mjs --test --test-force-exit test/wallet-nav-enablement.spec.ts test/wallet-page.spec.ts test/wallet-ops-logic.spec.ts  # cwd: apps/web
pnpm --filter @apps/portal run test:certify:wallet-ws1
pnpm --filter @apps/web run test:certify:wallet-ws1
pnpm run guard:import-boundary && pnpm run guard:wallet-core-boundary
pnpm --filter @apps/api run guard:tenant-isolation && pnpm --filter @apps/api run guard:rls-session-local
```

Optional: skip redundant package builds when deps are already built — `WALLET_CERT_SKIP_BUILD=1` on the smoke server script. Reuse running API/web/portal when health endpoints respond (Playwright `reuseExistingServer`, default locally).

## 9. Phase 1 — Denali workspace enablement (manifest + capability only)

Phase 1 adds **workspace-level** Wallet support for Denali without activating Wallet for any Denali tenant. This is distinct from tenant rollout (Phase 2+).

### 9.1 Workspace vs tenant gates

| Layer                               | Denali Phase 1 state                                                                                                               | Gate code when blocked                                                                    |
| ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Workspace support**               | `workspaceWallet.supported: true` in `packages/workspaces/denali/workspace.manifest.json`                                          | `WALLET_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED` (unsupported workspaces only, e.g. `urban`)                |
| **Tenant module enablement**        | **Not activated** — no Denali seed or dev tenant theme adds `"wallet"` to `enabledModules`; `defaultModuleEnabledWhenUnset: false` | `FORBIDDEN_WALLET_MODULE_DISABLED`                                                        |
| **Operator `walletNav` capability** | `capabilities.walletNav.supported: true` in `denali.plugin.ts`                                                                     | Nav/route still hidden until tenant module enablement passes (`ensureWalletNavSupported`) |

Workspace support and tenant enablement are **independent**:

- A supported workspace with wallet omitted from theme → API/portal fail closed with `FORBIDDEN_WALLET_MODULE_DISABLED`.
- An unsupported workspace → `WALLET_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED` regardless of theme.

### 9.2 Denali manifest bindings (Phase 1)

| Field                           | Value                                          | Notes                                                                               |
| ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `supported`                     | `true`                                         | Product declares Denali can host Wallet                                             |
| `defaultModuleEnabledWhenUnset` | `false`                                        | Unlike `wallet-ws1`, Denali does **not** auto-enable when `enabledModules` is empty |
| `capabilities.memberAccounts`   | `true`                                         | Member stored-value accounts (when tenant-enabled)                                  |
| `capabilities.ops`              | `true`                                         | Operator reconciliation UI (when tenant-enabled)                                    |
| `capabilities.gatewayTopUp`     | `false`                                        | Out of scope Phase 1                                                                |
| `capabilities.withdrawals`      | `false`                                        | Out of scope Phase 1                                                                |
| `capabilityRevision`            | `1`                                            | MAT-001 revision pin                                                                |
| `ledgerPolicy`                  | `./wallet` → `DenaliWalletLedgerPolicyAdapter` | Manifest-bound placeholder; no finance-core import                                  |
| `opsManifest`                   | `./wallet` → `DEFAULT_WALLET_OPS_MANIFEST`     | Theme resolver stub; no runtime ops                                                 |
| HTTP routes                     | `WALLET_HTTP_ROUTE_MANIFEST` group             | Handler package `@app-tour/wallet-http` (same as certification fixture)             |

`versionPins.capabilityPins.workspaceWallet.revision: 1` aligns codegen capability versioning with the block revision.

### 9.3 Refund and finance terminology (unchanged)

| Concept               | Phase 1 contract                                                                                                           |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Refund-to-wallet**  | **Manual in v1** — operator credit via Wallet ops when tenant-enabled; no automatic `completeRefund` → member wallet write |
| **`bookingWalletId`** | Registration finance GL identifier in `packages/workspaces/denali/src/finance/` — **not** a member wallet account id       |
| **`walletNetMinor`**  | Finance invoice/reporting field only — **not** member wallet balance                                                       |

Phase 1 does not modify `finance-core`, Denali registration-finance semantics, refund automation, checkout Wallet payment, holds, gateway top-up, withdrawals, or P2P transfers.

### 9.4 Verification (Phase 1 isolated)

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry --check
pnpm --filter @apps/api run test:file -- src/workspace-wallet/wallet-contract-certification.spec.ts
pnpm --filter @apps/api run test:file -- src/workspace-wallet/wallet-http-route-registration.spec.ts
pnpm --filter @apps/web run test:file -- test/thin-shell-wallet-nav-capability.spec.ts
pnpm run guard:import-boundary
pnpm run guard:wallet-core-boundary
git diff --check
```

Negative paths preserved: unsupported workspace → `WALLET_WORKSPACE_UNSUPPORTED`; supported workspace without wallet theme → `FORBIDDEN_WALLET_MODULE_DISABLED`. E2E `WALLET-CERT-D01` (Denali club smoke `denali.admin.localhost` / tenant `…000003`) remains valid — **only** the isolated pilot tenant enables Wallet.

## 10. Phase 2 — Denali pilot tenant activation (dev/cert only)

Phase 2 activates Wallet for **one** Denali dev/cert tenant. All other Denali tenants (club smoke `…000003`, operator smoke `…000014`, production rows) remain wallet-disabled.

### 10.1 Pilot identity (non-secret)

| Field                | Value                                                                |
| -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Tenant id**        | `00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000430`                               |
| **Subdomain**        | `denali-wallet-pilot`                                                |
| **Workspace type**   | `denali`                                                             |
| **Admin host**       | `admin.denali-wallet-pilot.localhost:3000`                           |
| **Portal host**      | `portal.denali-wallet-pilot.localhost:3003`                          |
| **Constants export** | `packages/workspaces/denali/src/smoke/denali-wallet-pilot-tenant.ts` |
| **Fixture SoT**      | `apps/api/test/fixtures/denali-wallet-pilot-tenant.ts`               |

### 10.2 Tenant theme (module + commerce currency)

Postgres `tenants.theme` for the pilot tenant only:

```json
{
  "enabledModules": ["wallet"],
  "portalModuleGrants": ["wallet"],
  "defaultLocale": "fa",
  "commerce": {
    "currency": "IRR",
    "paymentMode": "offline_receipt",
    "gatewayProvider": null,
    "frozen": true
  }
}
```

Member API currency authority: `theme.commerce.currency` → `IRR` (zero-decimal display). **No** hardcoded Denali currency inside `wallet-core`.

**Operator / portal surface gating:** `GET /api/v2/tenant-config` merges branding from `resolveRegisteredTenantById` with **raw** Postgres `tenants.theme` capability fields (`enabledModules`, `portalModuleGrants`, `commerce`) via `mergeTenantConfigSurfaceTheme`. Denali sets `defaultModuleEnabledWhenUnset: false` in workspace wallet bindings — without `enabledModules` in the tenant-config payload, operator Wallet nav stays hidden even when the DB row is correct. Finance uses the same raw-theme pattern (`findTenantFinanceWorkspaceRow`); wallet surfaces consume the merged tenant-config theme.

| Member                                 | Membership `portalModuleGrants` | Portal `/me/wallet`        | API `/wallet/me/*`                 |
| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Entitled pilot member                  | `["wallet"]`                    | Allowed                    | Allowed                            |
| Non-entitled pilot member              | `[]`                            | `MemberModuleUnauthorized` | Account isolation by `user_id`     |
| Any member on `denali` smoke `…000003` | n/a                             | No wallet nav              | `FORBIDDEN_WALLET_MODULE_DISABLED` |

### 10.3 Seeding (Postgres only)

Idempotent script: `apps/api/scripts/seed-denali-wallet-pilot.ts`

1. `ProvisioningService.seedDenaliWalletPilotTenant()` — upsert pilot row (`workspaceType: denali`, wallet theme above).
2. Owner + entitled/denied members via Prisma admin + `withTenantRls`.
3. Wallet account + deterministic IRR credit/debit history via `PrismaWalletRepository`.
4. **Does not** modify `denali` smoke tenant `…000003` or operator smoke `…000014`.

```bash
NODE_ENV=development DATABASE_URL=... DATABASE_URL_ADMIN=... \
  pnpm --filter @apps/api run seed:denali-wallet-pilot
```

### 10.4 Manual refund-to-wallet SOP (v1 — no automation)

Automatic refund → member wallet is **out of scope**. Operators follow this sequence when finance approves a refund that should land in the member Wallet:

1. **Complete the finance refund first** in the finance command center (existing refund flow; no wallet write).
2. **Credit the member Wallet manually** from the operator `/wallet` panel (pilot tenant only until broader rollout).
3. **Include `refundId` in the reason/reference** field so support can correlate ledger rows with finance.
4. **Use a stable `Idempotency-Key`** per intended credit (e.g. `refund-to-wallet:{refundId}`) so retries replay safely without double-credit.

No checkout Wallet payment, gateway top-up, withdrawal, hold, P2P, or `completeRefund` → wallet automation in Phase 2.

### 10.5 Verification (Phase 2 isolated)

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry --check
pnpm --filter @app-tour/wallet-core run test
pnpm --filter @app-tour/wallet-http run test
pnpm --filter @app-tour/wallet-http-contracts run test
pnpm --filter @apps/api run test:wallet-postgres-certification
pnpm --filter @apps/portal run test:certify:denali-wallet-pilot
pnpm --filter @apps/web run test:certify:denali-wallet-pilot
pnpm --filter @apps/web run test:certify:wallet-ws1   # includes WALLET-CERT-D01 negative
pnpm run guard:import-boundary && pnpm run guard:wallet-core-boundary
```
